      "text": "If a visual indicator is necessary for the clinician to identify the equipment or part of the equipment that requires clinician response or awareness, at least one visual alarm signal 53 shall be provided that:\n1. indicates the priority of the highest priority alarm condition; and\n2. can be perceived correctly at a distance of 4 m from the PCA pump.\n(IEC 60601-1-8 2.3.1)",
